A||||7||skitime||1988 GT steering rack turns lock to lock?||||1||
Z||000000||skitime||11-27-2000||10:53 PM||||I was discussing with someome with a 87 GT that there is a difference between GT and Formula in the number of turns lock to lock. 3 turns for the Formula and 3 1/2 for the GT.  Is this true and is it the same for the 88 GT?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Bob Englert||11-27-2000||11:18 PM||||That is not what I said Skitime!<P>As far as I know, the GT and Formula used the 3 turn rack.  The coupes used a 3 1/2 turn rack.<P>I do know that all 84's used a 3 turn rack wheich was changed to 3 1/2 turn for 85 and later for the coupes, sport coupes, and SE's.  The GT stayed with the 3 turn rack.  It is possible that some SE's with the WS6 option used the 3 turn rack.<P>Welcome other info if I am wrong here.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000002||skitime||11-27-2000||11:27 PM||||Sorry if I got it wrong. What I was really trying to get to is this - could I put a 3 1/2 rack in an 88 GT? Any idea why the SE had the 3 1/2 rack. Bob, are the racks interchangable with the 88 and are both available at the parts supply store? Thanks<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||MrPBody||11-28-2000||08:51 AM||||Based on what I have read (I have no direct knowledge):<P>'88 front suspension and steering, including the rack, is different from '84 - '87.  I don't know if the entire rack can be interchanged.<P>The lower-ratio (3-turn?) rack is part of WS6 suspension option.  It gives quicker steering at the cost of higher effort.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Bob Englert||11-28-2000||10:47 AM||||The 88 racks are NOT interchangable with the 84-87 racks.<P>There is no external difference between a 3 and 3 1/2 turn rack.  As long as you are getting the correct year, they are interchangable.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000005||skitime||11-28-2000||03:23 PM||||Do they make a 3 1/2 rack that would fit an 88 GT?  I think my lady would appreciate less steering effort on her car since her broken back. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Bob Englert||11-28-2000||10:11 PM||||Does someone on the forum have an 88 coupe.  If so, could they count the number of turns of the wheel from end to end.  If they give you 3 1/2 turns then you will have your answer.  <P>If so, check with Kicj Hill or Ed Parks to see if you can get a rack for an 88 coupe for your GT.  The Fiero store also sells remanufactured racks for the 88.  They should be able to tell you if they are 3 or 3 1/2 turns.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000007||Raydar||11-29-2000||12:46 AM||||FWIW... The Fiero Store only lists one rack for the 88. Several different part #s for the 84-87s.||||reg||1
